    "answer": {
      "short": "Strictly, only the third statement is correct: $[3,4]$ is a set. The first two are statements about $x$.",
      "worked": "A domain is a set, so only “The domain is $[3,4]$” is strictly correct. The inequality $3\\le x\\le 4$ states a condition on $x$, and $x\\in[3,4]$ states that $x$ belongs to the interval. Neither expression names the set itself, although both communicate the intended restriction.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
